+
+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts `{ "csv": "..." }` with columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. `soldAt` is an ISO instant with a timezone;
+  `qty` is a positive quantity with at most three decimal places. Each unit
+  sold uses one recipe portion. Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`,
+  counting distinct new tickets and the sum of their sold quantities.
+  All rows of previously imported tickets are skipped. Rows of a new ticket
+  in the same file are all imported. Any invalid row or shortage rejects the
+  whole file with `bad_request` naming the CSV row (first data row is 2).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 3, "actual": 4, "variance": 1 }`.
+  Dates are inclusive UTC days; `from` must not follow `to`. Theoretical use
+  uses ingredient quantities captured at import, actual use includes every
+  `consume` movement, and variance is actual minus theoretical. Only items
+  with positive theoretical or actual use are listed, ordered by item id.
